Hi,

Beth Friedman writes:

> But failing that kind of luck, what do you recommend for my hapless
> tourists to wield?

My tourists always grab the very first weapon they can find, figuring
that anything is better than hand to hand combat.  My ascended tourist
actually started with a cursed long sword and went on to a cursed
silver saber.

> Daggers are easy to find, and are fairly easy to get to Basic on.  I
> tried mace and flail when I found those, and was able to get to
> Basic, but that's where it maxes out.

Tourists can get to expert in dagger, and I would recommend that you
raise this skill as quickly as possible.  Those points are not wasted,
as daggers provide an excellent ranged attack throughout the game.

> Is there any particular weapon that tourists are best at, or are
> they just sort of mediocre at everything?

Tourists can get skilled in saber, long sword, and two-weaponing,
which makes them positively devastating.  Think Grayswandir or
Frostbrand, dual-wielded silver saber, both weapons fully enchanted,
relevant skills maxed.

Another very nice option is Magicbane, both for hitting things and for
the spiffy effects.

